.TH "LIBPKGSTATE\-POSIX" "3" "" "libpkgstate\-posix" "Version 3.1.0"
.SH NAME
libpkgstate\-posix \- POSIX immutable\-generation storage for libpkgstate
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]#include <libpkgstate\-posix/libpkgstate\-posix.h>\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]libpkgstate\-posix\f[R] implements the abstract \f[B]libpkgstate\f[R] canonical\-store contract with one descriptor\-anchored immutable\-generation filesystem backend.
It owns store binding, publication locking, immutable generation publication, current\-selector replacement, durability reporting, recovery refusal, and explicit empty\-store bootstrap, and read\-only store diagnostics.
Canonical generation\-v1 record encoding and validation are provided by \f[B]libpkgstate\f[R] and consumed without reinterpretation.
.PP
The semantic \f[B]libpkgstate\f[R] owner retains stale comparison, result derivation, publication requests and receipts, and evidence codecs.
This provider cannot reinterpret a request, silently rebase stale authority, construct package state, or claim target\-filesystem and state\-store atomicity.
.SH INTERFACE
\f[B]pkgstate::posix::canonical_generation_store\f[R] opens or initializes one target\-bound store.
\f[B]open_existing()\f[R] validates an existing store without creating or repairing it.
The class implements \f[B]canonical_store\f[R] and therefore receives only the exact resulting snapshot derived by the non\-virtual core publication sequence.
.SH TOOLS
\f[B]pkgstate\-init\f[R](1) is the explicit empty\-state bootstrap client.
\f[B]pkgstate\-check\f[R](1) is the read\-only diagnostic client.
Both are built by default and installed only when \f[B]install_tools\f[R] is enabled.
